                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="26-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_sg.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Shotgun" title="Shotgun" ></span>Audio-Technica AT4073a</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Shotgun Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The AT4071a is a short (9.3&#39;&#39;), lightweight shotgun microphone with a true condenser capsule and a patented interference tube that provides &#8220;directivity equal to mics up to 50% longer.&#8221;</p><p>The mic is also remarkable for its high sensitivity (70.8 mV/Pa) and low self-noise (14dBA). A switch on the mic body enables a high-pass filter (-12dB/octave @ 150 Hz).</p><p>According to Patent 4,789,044, most &#8220;shotgun&#8221; microphones attempt to narrow their pickup pattern by attaching an interference pipe to the face of a cardioid transducer, leaving the rear of the capsule is exposed (&#8220;positioned at a free audio sound field&#8221;).</p><blockquote><p><cite>Patent 4,789,044</cite></p><p>[This arrangement] has a defect and drawback [in] that it picks up wind noise and raises a proximity effect which distorts [the] low-band area when the sound source is near.</p></blockquote><p>Audio-Technica&#8217;s innovation incorporates the following changes:</p><ul><li>The holes along the top of the interference tube are elongated, and covered with a polyvinylidene fluoride membrane; these work together to prevent resonance inside the pipe and to introduce a phase change.</li><li>The transducer is mounted toward the rear of the tube, but offset toward the front to allow space for additional vents in the tube behind the transducer.</li><li>The outside diameter of the microphone capsule is smaller than the inside diameter of the interference tube, allowing the spaces before and behind the capsule to be acoustically mated.</li><li>Most, possibly all of the vents in the interference tube are covered with a &#8220;non-woven textile,&#8221; presumably to reduce wind noise.</li></ul><p>See also the AT4071a, a longer version of the same microphone, with higher sensitivity and lower self-noise.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Audio-Technica/AT4073a">Audio-Technica AT4073a</a> is also known as: AT4073.</p>
